  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 760325,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 1991 Du Ma Racing: A Galloping Good Time (or Gamble!)\n\nStep into the world of 1991 Du Ma Racing, a quirky and unlicensed horse racing game for the Nintendo Entertainment System! Developed by Idea-Tek and published by Super Mega in Taiwan, this title offers a unique blend of competitive racing and strategic betting.\n\nThe game features two distinct modes to satisfy different playstyles. In *Race Mode*, two players can test their reflexes and timing. By precisely pressing buttons, players build up their horse's power and unleash it for a speed boost, striving to outmaneuver their opponent and cross the finish line first. \n\nFor those who prefer a more relaxed approach, *Gamble Mode* allows up to six players to wager their starting credits (500 each) on five different horses. The race unfolds automatically, driven by AI, and players earn prize money based on their predictions. The ultimate goal? Accumulate more wealth than your fellow gamblers! 1991 Du Ma Racing delivers a simple yet engaging experience, perfect for casual gaming and friendly competition."
    },
